---
import DownloadButtons from "../../download/DownloadButtons.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Question from "../../guide/Question.astro";
import { leavesSite, RELEASES, sitePath } from "../../site/links.ts";
---

<GuidePage slug="install" lead="Answers to what comes up between downloading Katari and reading in it.">
  <Question id="which-file" question="Which file should I download?" open>
    <p>
      Katari runs on phones and tablets with Android 10 or newer. Most people want <strong>Katari</strong>. The
      same app without Google services is <strong>Katari FOSS</strong>, which never sends crash logs or usage data.
    </p>
    <DownloadButtons explained={false} />
    <p>
      Both come as smaller builds for one kind of processor too: arm64-v8a for most phones of recent years, and
      armeabi-v7a for older ones. They are on the <a href={`${RELEASES}/latest`} {...leavesSite()}>release page</a>.
    </p>
  </Question>

  <Question id="updates" question="Does Katari update itself?">
    <p>
      Yes, both builds do. When a new version is out, Katari offers to download and install it. Android asks once
      for permission to let Katari install apps.
    </p>
  </Question>

  <Question id="from-mihon" question="Can I bring my library over from Mihon?">
    <p>
      Yes. In Mihon, create a backup containing everything you want to keep, then choose it when Katari's setup
      offers <em>Move from Mihon</em>. Include private settings to bring source preferences and sign-ins along.
      <a href={sitePath("guide/backups-and-storage/#mihon")}>Backups and storage</a> walks through it.
    </p>
    <p>
      To keep your downloads, select the storage folder Mihon used. Extensions installed privately in Mihon need to
      be installed again.
    </p>
  </Question>

  <Question id="content" question="Where does the content come from?">
    <p>
      Katari comes with no content and has no affiliation with any provider. Sources are extensions you choose: add
      an extension store under Browse › Extensions, then install the extensions you want from it.
      <a href={sitePath("guide/first-steps/")}>First steps</a> walks through it.
    </p>
  </Question>

  <Question id="data-sent" question="What does Katari send, and can I turn it off?">
    <p>
      Katari can send anonymized crash logs and usage data. Its setup shows both as switches, and you can change
      them any time in Settings › Security and privacy. Katari FOSS sends neither.
    </p>
  </Question>
</GuidePage>
